.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3 Give a manager a quick view of where to focus so their folks stay clear on Required Clarity.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-3
    Required Clarity is a Gruuv Health category (Healthy / Warning / Needs Attention), same rules as 1:1 Hub Overview.
    This dashboard rolls those signals up per employee with action guidance for what to do next.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 How to read each row
  %p.mb-3
    The top bar shows Gruuv Health Required Clarity per item (Healthy, Warning, Needs Attention); the bottom bar shows what action to take next on each check-in.
    Hover any segment for details. Use refresh controls when data seems stale — they queue a Gruuv Health recalculation.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Example employee row
  .card.mb-3
    .card-header.py-2
      %strong Example
    .card-body.py-2
      .table-responsive
        %table.table.table-sm.mb-2
          %thead
            %tr
              %th Employee
              %th Aspirations
              %th Assignments
              %th Position
          %tbody
            %tr
              %td
                Alex Rivera
                %br
                %small.text-muted Casey Manager
              %td
                .check-in-health-bar.d-flex.rounded.overflow-hidden{style: "height: 16px; min-width: 80px;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-eh-warning{style: "width: 100%;"}
                .check-in-health-bar.d-flex.rounded.overflow-hidden.mt-1{style: "height: 6px; min-width: 80px;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-action-red{style: "width: 100%;"}
              %td
                .check-in-health-bar.d-flex.rounded.overflow-hidden{style: "height: 16px; min-width: 80px;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-eh-healthy{style: "width: 50%;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-eh-warning{style: "width: 50%;"}
                .check-in-health-bar.d-flex.rounded.overflow-hidden.mt-1{style: "height: 6px; min-width: 80px;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-action-green-striped{style: "width: 50%;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-action-orange{style: "width: 50%;"}
              %td
                .check-in-health-bar.d-flex.rounded.overflow-hidden{style: "height: 16px; min-width: 60px;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-eh-healthy{style: "width: 100%;"}
                .check-in-health-bar.d-flex.rounded.overflow-hidden.mt-1{style: "height: 6px; min-width: 60px;"}
                  .flex-grow-0.check-in-health-action-neon-green-striped{style: "width: 100%;"}
      .row.g-2.small
        .col-12.col-lg-6
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Top bars (taller) show Gruuv Health per required item.
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Bottom bars (shorter) show the recommended next action for each item.
        .col-12.col-lg-6
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Hover a segment for status, last finalized date, and next steps.
          %div
            %i.bi.bi-arrow-up-right.me-1
            Refresh controls should be used only when data seems stale/incorrect.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Status legend
  .row.mb-0
    .col-12.col-lg-6
      %p.fw-semibold.mb-2 Top bar (Gruuv Health Required Clarity)
      %ul.mb-3.mb-lg-0
        - [EngagementHealth::NEEDS_ATTENTION, EngagementHealth::WARNING, EngagementHealth::HEALTHY].each do |status|
          %li
            %span.d-inline-block.rounded-circle.me-2.align-middle{class: check_ins_health_eh_status_swatch_css(status), style: "width: 10px; height: 10px;"}
            %strong= EngagementHealth::STATUS_LABELS.fetch(status)
            = " - #{check_ins_health_engagement_status_meaning(status)}"
        %li
          %span.d-inline-block.rounded-circle.me-2.align-middle{class: check_ins_health_eh_status_swatch_css(CheckInsHealthBarsHelper::NEW_ASSIGNMENT_GRACE_DISPLAY), style: "width: 10px; height: 10px;"}
          %strong New assignment
          = " - #{check_ins_health_engagement_status_meaning(CheckInsHealthBarsHelper::NEW_ASSIGNMENT_GRACE_DISPLAY)}"
    .col-12.col-lg-6
      %p.fw-semibold.mb-2 Bottom bar (action-based)
      %ul.mb-0
        - check_ins_health_action_bar_legend_items.each do |legend|
          %li
            %span.d-inline-block.rounded-circle.me-2.align-middle{class: legend[:css], style: "width: 10px; height: 10px;"}
            %strong= legend[:color].humanize
            = " - #{legend[:label]}"
